From 6ad82b7b4690dc07b506ce08710b476b4efe12fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:34:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(capsule): return dedicated AlreadyRegistered errors for
 duplicate registrations

Duplicate capsule and uplink registrations were reported as
CapsuleError::UnsupportedEntryPoint, producing messages such as
"Unsupported entry point: Already registered: <id>" and forcing callers
to string-match to detect duplicates.

Add CapsuleError::AlreadyRegistered and
CapsuleError::UplinkAlreadyRegistered, return them from every duplicate
check in the registry, and name them in the `# Errors` docs. Add
regression tests for register, register_existing and register_uplink.

Closes #476
